# WSL/bash scripts and the node-pty patch MUST stay LF, even when cloned on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true — CRLF would break `bash` (\r errors) and stop patch-package from applying.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
# The contract suite is hundreds of static regexes over the shipped source, and several of them span lines — a
# CRLF checkout makes a handful report phantom failures naming plausible regressions, which invites someone to
# spend an afternoon debugging working code. Pin every file the suite reads to LF everywhere.
*.js    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
# test/e2e/fake-gh/gh — extensionless `#!/bin/sh` shim (see its own header comment for why it has no
# extension). Same *.sh reasoning above applies verbatim: a CRLF checkout breaks the shebang under git-bash.
# Not covered by the *.sh glob because it deliberately has no extension, so it needs its own line.
test/e2e/fake-gh/gh text eol=lf
# every file type the contract suite reads stays LF under core.autocrlf=true — unpinned .ps1/.md/.yml/.json made
# the suite's multi-line regexes checkout-dependent.
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
